---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Safeguarding"
  description="Safeguarding principles for children and adults at Charles Michael Sports Hub."
>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white py-20 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="section-subtitle text-red-brand">Safety Comes First</p>
      <h1 class="font-display font-black text-6xl md:text-8xl leading-none mb-6">Safeguarding</h1>
      <p class="font-body text-blue-100 text-xl max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        We want every person who trains, competes, or visits to be treated with dignity and to feel safe, respected, and welcome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-10">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="section-subtitle">Our Commitment</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mb-4">A Safe Place to Learn</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Charles Michael Sports Hub is committed to safeguarding children and adults at risk from abuse, neglect, bullying, discrimination, and avoidable harm. Everyone involved in our activities shares responsibility for maintaining safe and respectful conduct.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <article class="card p-6 reveal">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-navy mb-3">Expected conduct</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-gray-600">
            <li>Use respectful, age-appropriate language and behaviour.</li>
            <li>Do not use physical punishment, humiliation, intimidation, or bullying.</li>
            <li>Respect personal boundaries and obtain appropriate consent before physical assistance.</li>
            <li>Raise safety concerns promptly and take them seriously.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card p-6 reveal">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-navy mb-3">Working with young people</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-gray-600">
            <li>Keep interactions open, appropriate, and focused on training.</li>
            <li>Use official channels for communication about young athletes.</li>
            <li>Do not take or share a child's image or personal information without appropriate permission.</li>
            <li>Follow agreed sign-in, collection, and supervision arrangements.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-bluegrey border-l-4 border-red-brand p-7 rounded-r-xl reveal">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Reporting a Concern</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
          If someone is in immediate danger, contact the appropriate emergency services first. Otherwise, report concerns to the CMSH safeguarding lead as soon as possible. Do not promise secrecy; share information only with people who need it to help keep someone safe.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          The safeguarding lead's name, verified contact details, reporting procedure, and escalation contacts must be added before this policy is relied on operationally. Until then, contact details are not available on this page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Policy Review</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          This page sets out our safeguarding commitment and is not a substitute for a complete, approved safeguarding procedure. CMSH should review it with the safeguarding lead and relevant Kenyan authorities or qualified advisers, and update it when procedures or applicable requirements change.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
